## Key Analytical Notes

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>IGAAP vs. IFRS PAT divergence — largest single flag:</b> IGAAP statutory results show a <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">9MFY26 net loss of ₹214.35 Cr</span> (widened from a ₹7.44 Cr profit in 9MFY25) <doc_source>step10web3</doc_source>, while IFRS accounts show a <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">profit of ₹208.31 Cr</span> (up from ₹119.52 Cr in 9MFY24). This ~₹422 Cr swing is not a data error — it reflects fundamentally different recognition bases: IFRS 17 (risk-adjusted contractual service margin release) vs. the Indian GAAP revenue-account method, compounded by the IGAAP P&L directly absorbing the <b>EOM excess transfer (₹24.57 Cr for 9M)</b> against profit, a treatment IFRS does not mirror identically.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>EOM forbearance overhang remains unresolved:</b> The <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">36.33%</span> EOM ratio for 9MFY26 still breaches the IRDAI-allowed cap of 35.90%. FY25's EOM breach (39.22% on 1/n basis vs. 35.55% allowed) remains pending IRDAI forbearance approval — a live regulatory risk whose P&L impact the auditors describe as "presently indeterminate" in their Emphasis of Matter.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>Underlying profitability ratios corroborate deterioration:</b> Operating Profit Ratio worsened to <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">(8.37%)</span> for 9MFY26 vs. +2.53% in 9MFY25; Net Earning Ratio fell to <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">(4.76%)</span> vs. +0.20% — consistent with the IGAAP net loss, despite continued strong top-line momentum (Gross Direct Premium Growth Rate of <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">21.84%</span>).
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #1E3A8A;background:#EFF6FF;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<b>Genuine disclosure gaps, not omissions:</b> Claims ratio, standalone expense ratio, commission ratio, combined ratio, solvency ratio (numeric), and retail health market share are not explicitly published as named metrics in either the statutory IGAAP results or the IFRS statements reviewed — these typically appear only in the investor presentation deck, which was outside the scope of the five documents specified. Per the sourcing rules, these have been left blank rather than estimated.
</div>

**Solvency ratio note:** The filing explicitly states "the Solvency has been computed at the last day of the period," confirming the ratio is computed and monitored internally, but the numeric disclosure row appears to have been dropped from the extracted table — it is genuinely not retrievable from this document as captured.</ans>
